WEBVTT

00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:35.720
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Hello?

00:00:36.639 --> 00:00:40.314
<v><b>Rob:</b></v> Hello. Is that, uh, Jennifer Zielinski?

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:41.714
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Yes. Who’s that?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.509
<v><b>Rob:</b></v> This is Rob Walker.

00:00:44.153 --> 00:00:44.919
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> I’m sorry, who?

00:00:46.014 --> 00:00:50.349
<v><b>Rob:</b></v> Rob Walker. I work for London 24seven.

00:00:50.677 --> 00:00:54.234
We need to talk about your trip to London in March.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:59.152
Er, you arrive on the 12th of March and

00:00:59.786 --> 00:01:02.360
you leave on the 19th, is that right?

00:01:02.723 --> 00:01:05.957
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> I’m really sorry Mr. Walker…er, Rob,

00:01:06.257 --> 00:01:07.680
but I’m not at work.

00:01:07.681 --> 00:01:09.437
Today is a holiday here.

00:01:09.885 --> 00:01:10.712
<v><b>Rob:</b></v> A holiday?

00:01:11.127 --> 00:01:13.771
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Yes, you know, it’s Thanksgiving.

00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:17.207
I’m at my parent’s house, with my family.

00:01:18.087 --> 00:01:19.560
<v><b>Rob:</b></v> Thanksgiving. Of course.

00:01:19.687 --> 00:01:20.633
Sorry.

00:01:20.946 --> 00:01:22.746
We don’t have Thanksgiving in England.

00:01:23.357 --> 00:01:24.177
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> No problem.

00:01:24.648 --> 00:01:28.051
Listen, call me on Monday at work.

00:01:28.464 --> 00:01:31.105
No, not Monday, Tuesday.

00:01:32.331 --> 00:01:35.681
<v><b>Rob:</b></v> Tuesday the third of December?

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:36.520
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Yes.

00:01:36.578 --> 00:01:38.889
<v><b>Jenny’s mom:</b></v> Jenny! Hurry up!

00:01:39.489 --> 00:01:40.915
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Talk to you on Tuesday.

00:01:41.196 --> 00:01:42.183
Thanks for calling.

00:01:42.663 --> 00:01:43.230
<v><b>Rob:</b></v> Bye.

00:01:43.798 --> 00:01:44.339
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Bye.